  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved maritime security reduces insurance costs, rerouting and transit delays for freight carrying advanced semiconductor modules and finished accelerator racks, easing logistical constraints and lowering supply pressure on advanced chips.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_hormuz_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_transformati</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_hormuz_conflict::maritime_security" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_pressure_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">A degradation in Persian Gulf maritime security forces Western (especially US/UK) naval assets to reallocate to Gulf/Indian Ocean protection, temporarily reducing deterrent posture or patrol density in the Black Sea/Eastern Europe and creating windows for increased Russian military activity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_hormuz_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_hormuz_conflict::maritime_security" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::compromised_hardware_rat" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Attacks, seizures and interdictions in the Strait of Hormuz force shippers to reroute, transship, or use third‑party brokers and fill gaps with rapid purchases from non‑vetted suppliers, increasing opportunities for physical tampering or insertion of compromised components into the global hardware flow.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_hormuz_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_hormuz_conflict::maritime_security" target="us_trade_coercion::policy_uncertainty_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved maritime security (escorts, deconfliction, reduced attacks) lessens pressure on policymakers to impose emergency trade restrictions or export controls, thereby reducing near‑term uncertainty among firms about future trade policy enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_hormuz_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_coercion</data>
</edge>
