<edge source="iran_hormuz_conflict::kinetic_escalation" target="ai_economic_transformati::ai_investment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising military strikes and force employment in the Hormuz theatre increase market volatility and perceived project risk, causing venture and corporate investors to delay or reallocate capital away from capital‑intensive AI projects, reducing the rate of new AI investment.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_hormuz_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_transformati</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_hormuz_conflict::kinetic_escalation" target="russia_ukraine_war::backchannel_activity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in kinetic incidents around Hormuz raises the risk of wider US‑Iran confrontation, prompting increased low‑visibility diplomatic contacts among Western capitals, Moscow, and Kyiv to manage spillover risks and deconflict across theatres.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_hormuz_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_hormuz_conflict::kinetic_escalation" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::detection_attribution" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in kinetic confrontations around Hormuz triggers accelerated US/allied intelligence, cyber‑forensics funding and interagency data‑sharing to track responsible actors, directly improving intrusion detection and attribution tooling and processes relevant to the US–China tech competition.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_hormuz_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_hormuz_conflict::kinetic_escalation" target="us_trade_coercion::reciprocal_retaliation" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in kinetic escalation (strikes on ships or military exchanges) lead the U.S. to rapidly increase the intensity and frequency of punitive economic measures (sanctions, secondary sanctions, trade penalties) in direct response, raising reciprocal retaliation intensity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_hormuz_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_coercion</data>
</edge>
