<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="ai_economic_transformati::regulatory_restrictions" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater policy alignment among allied states leads to coordinated technology controls and harmonized restrictions on exports, data flows and platform access, increasing the overall stringency of AI-related regulation across jurisdictions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_transformati</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="iran_hormuz_conflict::econ_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater policy alignment and coordination among Western allies driven by the Russia–Ukraine crisis enables quicker, unified sanctions and secondary‑sanctions measures against actors involved in Hormuz disruptions, increasing economic pressure on those networks.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::corporate_cyber_investme" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater policy alignment among Western allies in response to the war produces coordinated threat advisories, procurement standards, and regulatory pressure that compel firms in the U.S. and partner markets to increase private-sector investment in cyber hardening and resilience.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="us_trade_coercion::tariff_escalation_speed" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater policy alignment among the US and like-minded partners enables coordinated, faster implementation of tariff increases and synchronized trade measures against targeted actors, accelerating the pace of tariff escalation.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_coercion</data>
</edge>
