<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::compromised_hardware_rat" target="ai_economic_transformati::chip_supply_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Widespread discovery of compromised or backdoored hardware prompts large buyers (cloud providers, defense contractors, hyperscalers) to reject affected vendors and shift purchases to a smaller set of vetted suppliers, creating immediate demand imbalance and delivery bottlenecks for advanced accelerators.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_transformati</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::compromised_hardware_rat" target="ai_economic_transformati::regulatory_restrictions" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">High prevalence of compromised components leads governments to impose procurement bans, mandatory security certifications, and export controls for hardware used in AI systems, tightening the legal and compliance regime around AI-related supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_economic_transformati</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::compromised_hardware_rat" target="iran_hormuz_conflict::maritime_security" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased prevalence of backdoored or compromised communications, navigation, and port-control hardware enables exploitation (e.g., AIS spoofing, terminal ICS manipulation) that directly degrades safe passage and incident response for ships in the Strait of Hormuz.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_conflict</data>
</edge>
