<edge source="ai_economic_transformati::regulatory_restrictions" target="russia_ukraine_war::intel_sharing_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter export controls and data‑flow/privacy regulations constrain cross‑border transfer of raw sensor data, models and processing tools, directly reducing the volume and speed of intelligence products exchanged between allies supporting Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_economic_transformati</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_economic_transformati::regulatory_restrictions" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::detection_attribution" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter cross‑border data and export restrictions reduce the volume and timeliness of forensic telemetry sharing and joint investigations, degrading detection coverage and the speed/accuracy of attribution.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_economic_transformati</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_economic_transformati::regulatory_restrictions" target="us_trade_coercion::policy_uncertainty_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Rapid tightening or expansion of AI export controls and data‑flow regulations creates ambiguity about permissible cross‑border transactions and compliance costs, directly increasing firms' uncertainty about future trade policy.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_economic_transformati</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_coercion</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_economic_transformati::regulatory_restrictions" target="us_trade_coercion::reciprocal_retaliation" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Introduction or expansion of unilateral AI‑related export controls and compliance rules provokes affected trade partners to respond with countermeasures (tariffs, restrictions or targeted sanctions), increasing the intensity and frequency of reciprocal retaliation.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_economic_transformati</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_coercion</data>
</edge>
